        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {},
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Query Intent Response"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY_INTENT_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1763113186139",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763113186141_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Map and Return the Following Output Structure:\n\n1. IsPayload:\nSet this value to false.\n\n2. Message:\nUsing the current allocations retrieved from the REST response at:\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_CURRENT_ALLOCATIONS.$output}}\n\n\nAnswer the user query originating from:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n(Important: The term personal contributions / individual compensation / IC / awards / records / allocations are used interchangeably to refer to allocations. It is NOT a classification.)\n\nThe response should have two parts:\n- A polite, user-friendly paragraph summarising the answer. If answer involves dates or monetary values, those should be formatted based on locale.\n\n- Show ONLY the relevant allocation/s which were used to deduce the answer in an HTML table following all rules below. If there are no allocations, don't render the table.\n\n** HTML Formatting Rules (Mandatory)\nYou must include a <style> block before the table that enforces:\n<style>\n  table {\n    border-collapse: collapse;\n    width: 100%;\n    font-size: 16px;\n  }\n  th, td {\n    border: 1px solid #ccc;\n    padding: 6px 8px;\n    vertical-align: middle;\n  }\n  .plan-line1 {\n    font-size: 16px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n    line-height: 0.1;\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0;\n  }\n  .plan-line2 {\n    font-size: 15px;\n    line-height: 0.1;\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0;\n  }\n  .plan-line3 {\n    font-size: 14px;\n    line-height: 0.1;\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0;\n  }\n</style>\nThis ensures consistent font sizes, minimal line spacing, and stable layout across all responses.\n\n** Columns and Attribute Mapping\nYour table should contain the following three columns:\n\n* Plan Details\n\nDisplayed as three stacked lines inside the same cell:\nLine 1 — {PlanName} in bold (.plan-line1)\nLine 2 — {ComponentName} in smaller font (.plan-line2)\nLine 3 — even smaller font (.plan-line3) showing date(s):\n\nFormatting rules for Line 3:\nIf {ProcessingType} = N\nShow: {EffectiveStartDate}\nOtherwise\nShow: {EffectiveStartDate} - {EffectiveEndDate}\nIf {EffectiveEndDate} = 4712-12-31\nShow: {EffectiveStartDate} - Ongoing\nFormat dates based on user locale\n\nLine spacing must remain minimal (controlled via CSS above).\n\n* Value or Amount\nIf {ValueFormat} = CURRENCY\nDisplay {ValueString} {DisplayCurrency}, where {ValueString} is formatted using currency precision defined by {DisplayCurrency}\nElse\nDisplay {ValueString} optionally followed by {NonMonetaryUOM} if that field is not null\nIf {ValueFormat} = NUMBER\nFormat {ValueString} as a localized number\n\n* Processing Type\nIf {ProcessingType} = N → display Once\nElse → display Recurring\n\n** Additional Requirements\n\nThe HTML table must be valid, well-formatted, use borders, and include one row per allocation record.\n\nThe table should show the allocations which are relevant to the query, not all allocations.\n\nDo not add extra descriptive text around the table.\n\nDo not invent data; use only what is available in the REST response.\n\nDo NOT mention internal action codes, system logic, or technical details.\n\nDo NOT suggest workarounds or imply how permissions can be bypassed.\n\nDo NOT invent, assume, or infer any information.\n\nDo NOT ask followup queries or suggest actions. \n\nReturn only the final message text.\n\nIf the user is not asking for contribution/allocation details, answer normally without generating any table.\n\nIf no allocation records exist in {{$context.$nodes.GET_CURRENT_ALLOCATIONS.$output}}, respond with something polite like\n\nYou currently have no active personal contributions or allocations.\n\n3. BatchPayload:\nReturn an empty array []"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"BatchPayload\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"Message\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"IsPayload\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
