          },
          "code": "CHECK_ELIGIBILITY_RESPONSE",
          "id": "1763133524973",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1763133524976_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Map and Return the Following Output Structure:\n\n1. IsPayload:\nSet this value to false.\n\n2. Message:\nThe message (Without any greetings like Dear Customer, Hello User, etc) must be valid HTML (without any header tags) and should contain three parts:\n  - A polite, user-friendly message to inform the user that they are eligible for plan: {{$context.$variables.RecordDetails.PlanDetails.PlanName}} and option: {{$context.$variables.RecordDetails.PlanDetails.ComponentName}} \n\n  - If and only if information is present in: {{$context.$variables.RecordDetails.PlanDetails.PlanInfo}}, include a short, clear and plain-text summary based on that the information.\n\n  - If and only if {{$context.$variables.RecordDetails.IsSupported}} is true, inform the user that they can create new allocations for the plan using the below template:\n    ***\n    Opening Line: \"You can create a new allocation for this plan using the template below:\" or something similar\n\n    Transform the JSON object provided in {{$context.$variables.RecordDetails.EntryTemplate}} into HTML.\n\n    Formatting Rules:\n    a. Show the \"Header\" inside <strong>.\n    b. Then show the fields as html list in this exact order:\n       - Plan:\n       - Option:\n       - Start Date:\n       - End Date: (only if available in Entry Template)\n       - Input Values\n    c. Under Input Values, list each input value:\n         - {Name}: {Value}\n    d. Preserve all text exactly, including phrases like \"(Do not modify)\".\n    e. Important: Output only HTML, no markdown, no extra commentary.\n    ***\n\n  - If and only if {{$context.$variables.RecordDetails.IsSupported}} is false, provide user friendly message to inform the user that the plan is not supported for transaction using this agent because: {{$context.$variables.RecordDetails.Reason}}. They need to use the UI flow to make changes for this plan.\n\n\n3. BatchPayload:\nReturn an empty array []"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"BatchPayload\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {}\n            }\n        },\n        \"Message\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"IsPayload\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
